1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,610
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:04,960
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,160
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,870
I've been an elevator
mechanic

5
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:09,250
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:11,530
Climbing ladders in
elevator shafts

7
00:00:11,530 --> 00:00:13,290
and kneeling in machine
rooms.

8
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,410
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:15,860
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,780
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:19,900
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,550
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:22,300
and it went away.

14
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:23,520
This is different.

15
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:24,520
Tight.

16
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,210
Full.

17
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,230
Like a band around

18
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:28,070
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:29,260
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,620
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:31,690
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,880
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,160
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,040
At three months,

25
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,040
give it six.

26
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,080
At six months,

27
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,610
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:40,670
At a year,

29
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:42,620
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,090
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,490
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,190
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:48,380
Every session,

34
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:49,810
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,050
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:52,670
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,710 --> 00:00:54,430
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,770
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:58,070
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:58,070 --> 00:00:59,120
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,210
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:02,150
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,900
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,110
And after that,

45
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:06,680
a second operation to go
back

46
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,720
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:08,650
I said no.

48
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:09,940
Every morning

49
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,510
I laced up my work boots

50
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:12,470
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:14,240
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,610
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:17,970
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:19,690
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:21,390
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:21,390 --> 00:01:22,600
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,190
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:25,680
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

59
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,010
game without shifting
every two minutes.

60
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:29,700
I'd climb down into an
elevator

61
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,150
pit and wonder how I'd

62
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:32,560
get back up the ladder.

63
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:34,140
Thirty years in, and I

64
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:35,140
didn't know how many more

65
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:36,510
shafts I had in me.

66
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:37,900
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,450
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:39,450 --> 00:01:40,540
like getting in the car

69
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,790
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:42,860
into a decision.

71
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:44,150
After a long and serious

72
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:45,570
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:47,300
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:48,880
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,360
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,180
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,540
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,900
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,870
nothing wrong.

80
00:01:58,230 --> 00:01:59,440
Only this time

81
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,640
there was no new number.

82
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,820
Nobody said

83
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,550
give it another six
months.

84
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:05,340
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:06,850
I sat in my truck

86
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:08,700
in the parking lot for a
while.

87
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:09,880
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:11,450
Then explain this.

89
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,700
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,070
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,390
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

92
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,410
I had a service call at
seven.

93
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:21,500
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,390
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:24,640
with my leg up,

96
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,320
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,590
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:29,210
was wrapped around my knee

99
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:30,200
and tightening.

100
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:32,610
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,510
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,850
And I just thought,

103
00:02:35,850 --> 00:02:37,560
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,090
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:40,770
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:41,670
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:43,280
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:43,510 --> 00:02:45,110
And when I found one,

109
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:46,390
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:46,390 --> 00:02:47,800
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,910
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:50,230
out and went looking.

113
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,780
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:53,100
For an explanation.

115
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:54,770
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,770 --> 00:02:56,930
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:58,380
doctor videos,

118
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,720
medical animations.

119
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,430
And that's when I found a
video

120
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:02,940
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

121
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,020
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

122
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,080
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,360
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,780
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,120
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,210
The ice.

127
00:03:14,350 --> 00:03:16,060
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:17,660
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:18,810
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:20,910
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:22,790
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:23,810
It's a preview.

133
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,970
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:26,370
you this works fast.

135
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:27,350
It doesn't.

136
00:03:27,490 --> 00:03:29,420
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:30,490
and to look at what's
going

138
00:03:30,490 --> 00:03:31,910
on around your new knee

139
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:33,450
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:35,930
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:37,800
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,840
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,230
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:42,520
everything for me.

145
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:44,310
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,890
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:47,540
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:48,810
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,090
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:52,720
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:54,610
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:54,990 --> 00:03:56,970
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:58,530
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,340
He said,

155
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,230
think about a swollen foot

156
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:02,580
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:04,120
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,180
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,650
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:09,190
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:10,540
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,120
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,930
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,060
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:17,780
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:20,770
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,580
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,200
But in some people

169
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,760
that swelling can stay
switched

170
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,760
on far longer than
expected.

171
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,010
And swollen tissue takes
up more

172
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:31,810
room than calm tissue
does.

173
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:33,260
So when you bend,

174
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:34,910
that tissue gets
compressed.

175
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,020
When you straighten,

176
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:37,170
it gets pulled tight.

177
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,490
That's the band.

178
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:40,990
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

179
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:41,870
And you start being

180
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:42,670
the one who says,

181
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:43,430
you go ahead.

182
00:04:43,470 --> 00:04:44,480
I'll stay here.

183
00:04:44,670 --> 00:04:46,250
And that's exactly why so
much

184
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:47,410
of what I'd tried

185
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:48,450
hadn't worked.

186
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,830
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:51,710
around the knee.

188
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,920
Worth doing,

189
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,180
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:55,990
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:04:55,990 --> 00:04:57,130
taking up room.

192
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,690
A nerve block quiets

193
00:04:58,690 --> 00:05:00,360
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,050
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,350
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:05,350 --> 00:05:07,120
finally calms down,

197
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,950
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,550
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,930
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:15,020
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,200
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,070
After two years of this,

203
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:20,670
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:22,920
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:24,950
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:26,820
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:29,340
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,530
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:31,530 --> 00:05:34,350
gel knee pads, compression
braces,

210
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:36,640
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,670
and all any of it gave

212
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:38,730
me was an hour.

213
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:40,150
I even looked at going

214
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:42,070
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:44,230
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,760
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,280
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:47,350 --> 00:05:48,660
Then one night I went

219
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:49,930
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:51,600
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,250
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,100
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,570
comparing notes on
stiffness

224
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:58,610
and tightness nobody could
explain.

225
00:05:58,890 --> 00:06:00,810
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:02,580
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,460
This one device,

228
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:06,360
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,780
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,900
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:11,670
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:13,190
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:15,050
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:17,190
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:19,570
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:19,570 --> 00:06:20,580
that if I ever found

237
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:21,850
something that helped,

238
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:22,900
I'd say so.

239
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,090
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:26,540
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:29,040
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:30,910
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:33,010
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:33,170 --> 00:06:35,160
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,000
just to see what all

246
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,080
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,260
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:41,600
charge $200 a session for,

249
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:44,330
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:44,330 --> 00:06:45,270
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:46,430
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,140
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:50,320
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,450
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:52,450 --> 00:06:54,650
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,590
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:56,970 --> 00:06:58,790
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:00,320
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,500
Ninety days.

260
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:04,300
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,930
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:06,930 --> 00:07:08,580
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:08,770 --> 00:07:11,150
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:12,700
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,370
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:15,530
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:15,630 --> 00:07:16,940
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:19,120
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,110
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,840
and I'd done it for two
years.

271
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,130
The left one was carrying
the difference.

272
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:26,060
When it came,

273
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:28,120
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

274
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,190
because I'd been let down

275
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:31,000
too many times to get
excited.

276
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:32,790
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:34,670
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

278
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:36,290
More like it was coming
from inside

279
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,850
the knee and spreading
around it.

280
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:39,120
And that was it.

281
00:07:39,190 --> 00:07:40,700
That was the whole
experience.

282
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:41,940
When I took it off,

283
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:42,880
I'll be honest,

284
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,560
nothing dramatic had
happened.

285
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:46,490
And after what that video
said,

286
00:07:46,490 --> 00:07:48,560
that's exactly what I
expected.

287
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:50,290
What was different

288
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:51,390
was that for the first

289
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:53,180
time in two years

